# pr-body-cap — the ONE cap on a PR body's size, in BYTES.
#
# GitHub's limit for an issue or pull-request body is 65536 characters. BOTH readers
# of this cap count BYTES — the way `wc -c` does — and the number below is the ONE
# value either of them uses.
#
# It is read from here by BOTH readers of a body's size:
#   - `scripts/sync-pr-body.sh`         — the sync PR's own guard;
#   - `scripts/check-pr-body-diff.mjs`  — the gate the pre-push hook runs on EVERY body.
# One definition, two readers: the cap cannot drift between them (R2). A second copy
# of the number in either reader is a second cap, and the two would disagree the
# first time one of them is changed.
#
# The environment variable `GITHUB_BODY_MAX` overrides the number in BOTH readers —
# for a tighter local policy, or for a self-test that wants a small body. The
# override is not a second DEFINITION: the number itself lives here and only here.
#
# ── THE RULE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# It is stated HERE, once, and both readers implement exactly it.
#
#   - a line whose first non-blank character is `#` is a COMMENT;
#   - a line that is blank is BLANK;
#   - every other line is a CONTENT line, and this file holds EXACTLY ONE of them.
#
# That one content line, with its surrounding whitespace removed, is a positive
# integer and NOTHING ELSE: no trailing note, no second number on the same line, no
# interior space.
#
# So a file that is not exactly this is UNREADABLE, and BOTH readers refuse it
# loudly: a second content line is not a second reading of the cap, it is a cap
# nobody chose, and a cap that cannot be read must fail LOUD rather than be
# silently replaced by a default that is not this number.
#
# `scripts/check-pr-body-cap.mjs` proves the two readers agree: it runs BOTH of them
# against the SAME file — this one, which both must read as the same number, and
# mutated ones, which both must refuse. A rule only one reader implements is a cap
# that can drift, which is the defect this rule closes.
65536
